-- Consolidate schema drift.
-- Generated by `prisma migrate diff --to-schema prisma/schema.prisma` against
-- the DB state at the end of migration 20251212000000_repair_missing_objects.
-- The migration history was pruned/squashed at some point and dozens of
-- CREATE TABLE / CREATE TYPE statements were lost. This migration backfills
-- them idempotently so subsequent migrations (which assume these objects
-- exist) apply cleanly on fresh installs.
--
-- DROPs were stripped: schema.prisma no longer models a handful of legacy
-- tables (BatchOperation, OutOfSyncChapter, Queue, Settings, Task, etc.)
-- that earlier migrations created. Prisma is fine with extra tables in the
-- DB, and dropping them on a populated install would lose data.
--
-- Every statement here is idempotent. Foreign-key ADD CONSTRAINT statements
-- are wrapped in DO blocks that swallow duplicate_object errors, so this
-- migration can be re-applied against a DB that already has all the
-- schema-drift objects.

